syn_map:|        |       |     |This attribute exists to allow configuration of   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | Innovus from Genus.                              |
syn_map:|LBR-40  |Info   |    4|An unsupported construct was detected in this     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | library.                                         |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Check to see if this construct is really needed   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | for synthesis. Many liberty constructs are not   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | actually required.                               |
syn_map:|LBR-41  |Info   |  128|An output library pin lacks a function attribute. |
syn_map:|        |       |     |If the remainder of this library cell's semantic  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | checks are successful, it will be considered as a|
syn_map:|        |       |     | timing-model                                     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | (because one of its outputs does not have a valid|
syn_map:|        |       |     | function.                                        |
syn_map:|LBR-101 |Warning|    2|Unusable clock gating integrated cell found at the|
syn_map:|        |       |     | time of loading libraries. This warning happens  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | because a particular library cell is defined as  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'clock_gating_integrated_cell', but 'dont_use'   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | attribute is defined as true in the liberty      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | library. To make Genus use this cell for clock   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | gating insertion, 'dont_use' attribute should be |
syn_map:|        |       |     | set to false.                                    |
syn_map:|        |       |     |To make the cell usable, change the value of      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'dont_use' attribute to false.                   |
syn_map:|LBR-109 |Info   |    2|Set default library domain.                       |
syn_map:|LBR-162 |Info   |   52|Both 'pos_unate' and 'neg_unate' timing_sense arcs|
syn_map:|        |       |     | have been processed.                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Setting the 'timing_sense' to non_unate.          |
syn_map:|LBR-412 |Info   |    4|Created nominal operating condition.              |
syn_map:|        |       |     |The nominal operating condition is represented,   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | either by the nominal PVT values specified in the|
syn_map:|        |       |     | library source                                   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | (via nom_process,nom_voltage and nom_temperature |
syn_map:|        |       |     | respectively)                                    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | , or by the default PVT values (1.0,1.0,1.0).    |
syn_map:|LBR-516 |Info   |    2|Missing library level attribute.                  |
syn_map:|PHYS-12 |Warning|    4|The variant range of wire parameters is too large.|
syn_map:|        |       |     | An example of wire parameters are, a WIDTH for   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | layer, PITCH for layer, MINSPACING for layers,   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | etc.                                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Check the consistency of the parameters, and see  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | if you can ignore this message or you're using   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | different LEF file with wrong parameters.        |
syn_map:|PHYS-279|Warning|   16|Physical cell not defined in library.             |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Ensure that the proper library files are available|
syn_map:|        |       |     | and have been imported.                          |
syn_map:|PHYS-752|Info   |    2|Partition Based Synthesis execution skipped.      |
syn_map:|POPT-502|Warning|    4|Total power has skewed contributions from leakage |
syn_map:|        |       |     | and dynamic power.                               |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                        |
syn_map:|        |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the    |
syn_map:|        |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the design  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is not in the 'active period' but in 'idle mode',|
syn_map:|        |       |     | i.e. no dynamic power but only leakage power is  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | consumed. For a reasonable optimization across   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | dynamic and leakage power, leakage contribution  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | is expected to be above 5% and below 95%. A      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution of less than 5% will result in      |
syn_map:|        |       |     | limited leakage optimization and contribution of |
syn_map:|        |       |     | more than 95% will result in limited dynamic     |
syn_map:|        |       |     | optimization. Adjust                             |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.          |
syn_map:|SYNTH-4 |Info   |    1|Mapping.                                          |
syn_map:|TUI-32  |Warning|    1|This attribute will be obsolete in a next major   |
syn_map:|        |       |     | release.                                         |
syn_map:|        |       |     |Attribute, 'number_of_routing_layers' on root is  |
syn_map:|        |       |     | going to be obsoleted. Use root attribute        |
syn_map:|        |       |     | 'design_top_routing_layer' instead.              |
syn_map:|TUI-58  |Info   |  235|Removed object.                                   |
